---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Marketing Strategy | SEO, Competitive Analysis & Content Direction" description="SEO, competitive analysis, content direction, and keyword strategy. I direct the marketing. You execute it.">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Services","item":"https://codyasmith.com/services"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Marketing Strategy","item":"https://codyasmith.com/services/marketing-strategy"}]})} />

  <section class="pt-40 pb-24 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/services" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-neutral-500 text-sm hover:text-neutral-300 transition-colors duration-200 mb-8 group">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 group-hover:-translate-x-1 transition-transform duration-200" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M7 16l-4-4m0 0l4-4m-4 4h18" />
        </svg>
        All services
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
        <span class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em]">02</span>
        <div class="h-px bg-neutral-800 flex-1"></div>
      </div>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl md:text-7xl text-neutral-100 leading-[1.05] mb-6">
        Marketing Strategy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-neutral-500 italic text-sm tracking-wide mb-10">I direct it. You execute it.</p>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl" data-frame="default">
        Somebody told you to "do SEO." Somebody else said content marketing. Your brother-in-law thinks you need TikTok. You've been paying for Google Ads but you can't tell if they're working because the analytics were set up wrong in 2019 and nobody's touched them since. Meanwhile your competitor just showed up on page one for the keyword you thought was yours.
      </p>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
        Your business has momentum. The question isn't whether to invest in marketing. It's where. SEO, content, ads, social: there's opportunity in all of it, but you can't do everything at once. I look at where you are, where the market is moving, and build the roadmap to get there first.
      </p>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
        Somebody told you to "do SEO." Somebody else said content marketing. Your brother-in-law thinks you need TikTok. The analytics were set up wrong in 2019, your competitor just showed up on page one, and you can't tell if your ad spend is working. I sort through all of it and tell you what to do first.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-28 px-6 surface-1">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="mb-16">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Clarity</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">What this is and what it isn't.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 p-8 hover:border-amber-500/40 transition-colors duration-200">
          <p class="text-amber-400 text-xs tracking-[0.15em] uppercase mb-6">What you get</p>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-neutral-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              An SEO roadmap built on real keyword data
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Competitive analysis that names names
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Content briefs your writer can actually use
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Monthly calls to review priorities
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Quarterly reporting with real numbers
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Someone telling you what to stop doing
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 p-8 hover:border-amber-500/40 transition-colors duration-200">
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs tracking-[0.15em] uppercase mb-6">What I don't do</p>
          <ul class="space-y-4 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-neutral-500 mt-0.5">&#10005;</span>
              Run your social media
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-neutral-500 mt-0.5">&#10005;</span>
              Manage your ad campaigns
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-neutral-500 mt-0.5">&#10005;</span>
              Write your blog posts for you
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-neutral-500 mt-0.5">&#10005;</span>
              Hand you a one-time audit and disappear
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-neutral-500 mt-0.5">&#10005;</span>
              Give you vague advice you can't act on
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-neutral-500 mt-0.5">&#10005;</span>
              Bill a retainer for retainer's sake
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-28 px-6 surface-2">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="mb-16">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Process</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">Here's how it works.</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl" data-vibe="default">
          I start with the data, build the plan, and stay in the loop to adjust it as the market moves.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-vibe="beach">
          First I show you where you rank against the competition: who's outranking you, what they're doing, and where the openings are. Then we build the plan to take those positions.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 mt-4 max-w-2xl" style="display:none" data-vibe="mountain">
          I build the foundation that makes everything else work. Keyword research, site structure, content architecture, the systems-level decisions that compound over time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="relative">
        <div class="absolute left-6 md:left-8 top-0 bottom-0 w-px bg-gradient-to-b from-amber-500/40 via-amber-500/20 to-transparent"></div>

        <div class="space-y-16">
          <div class="relative pl-16 md:pl-20">
            <div class="absolute left-3 md:left-5 top-1 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500 bg-neutral-950 flex items-center justify-center">
              <span class="text-amber-400 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">1</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">I read everything.</h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-processing="default">
              Your site, your competitors' sites, the keywords you think you own and the ones you actually rank for. I pull the data, name the gaps, and write it all down. Nothing I recommend later will come from a hunch. It comes from this.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">
              Site crawl, content audit, competitive analysis, keyword universe with intent classification. Every finding ties to source data, so any recommendation that comes later traces back here.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">
              I get smart on your space, your competitors, and your keyword landscape before recommending anything. The audit document grounds every move that comes after.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="relative pl-16 md:pl-20">
            <div class="absolute left-3 md:left-5 top-1 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500/60 bg-neutral-950 flex items-center justify-center">
              <span class="text-amber-400/60 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">2</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">The audit becomes a plan with an order.</h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">
              Not everything matters equally, and some of the things you've been doing don't matter at all. I'll tell you what to do this month, what to do next quarter, and what to stop wasting money on immediately.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">
              A direction document. Where the marketing is heading, what it's heading toward, what to focus on first.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">
              A sequenced priority list. Each item dated and ranked, with the rationale written next to it. Hand it to anyone and they know what to do first.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="relative pl-16 md:pl-20">
            <div class="absolute left-3 md:left-5 top-1 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500/40 bg-neutral-950 flex items-center justify-center">
              <span class="text-amber-400/40 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">3</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">Then we talk once a month.</h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-processing="default">
              I show up with content briefs your writer can use, keyword targets worth chasing, and a clear answer to "what should we be doing right now?" You execute. I steer. When the data says the plan needs to change, I change it and tell you why.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">
              Each monthly call ends with named decisions: which content brief gets picked up next, which keyword target moves up the priority stack, which priority falls off the list. The "why" is written down so the next call has a starting point.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">
              We talk once a month. You leave knowing what to focus on next and why. The plan stays current because the data does.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="relative pl-16 md:pl-20">
            <div class="absolute left-3 md:left-5 top-1 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border-2 border-amber-500/20 bg-neutral-950 flex items-center justify-center">
              <span class="text-amber-400/20 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold">4</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">Every three months, the numbers go on the table.</h3>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" data-frame="default">
              Rankings, traffic, conversions, and what it all means. If something isn't working, I say so. You won't get a report that makes bad news sound like progress.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
              Every three months, the numbers go on the table. Where you gained ground, what's compounding, where the next bets are. The pages and priorities worth doubling down on.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
              Quarterly: what didn't move. The pages that flatlined, the keywords that lost position, the channels not earning their cost. The list of things to drop or rework.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-28 px-6 surface-1">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="mb-16">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Deliverables</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">What you walk away with.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 p-6 hover:border-amber-500/40 transition-colors duration-200">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Keyword research</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">Real search volume, real difficulty scores, grouped by intent. Not a spreadsheet dump. A prioritized list of opportunities.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">The keywords that define where your business shows up, and where it should. Prioritized by the opportunities that move the needle most.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">Search volume, keyword difficulty, intent mapping, and SERP feature analysis. Grouped by topic cluster with monthly search estimates and ranking probability.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 p-6 hover:border-amber-500/40 transition-colors duration-200">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Competitive analysis</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-phase="default">Who's ranking for what you want, what they're doing differently, and where the gaps are you can exploit.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="spring">A clear picture of who owns the search results you want and what it takes to overtake them.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-phase="fall">Domain authority comparisons, backlink gap analysis, content overlap mapping, and ranked list of exploitable keyword gaps with difficulty scores.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 p-6 hover:border-amber-500/40 transition-colors duration-200">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Content briefs</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-processing="default">Page-level briefs with target keywords, structure recommendations, and competitive context. Hand these to your writer.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">Briefs your writer can use. Keyword cluster sized, intent layered, content outline built around the SERP that's actually showing up. The questions that delay a draft, pre-answered.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">Briefs your writer can hand off and execute. They get a doc; you get a piece of content.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 p-6 hover:border-amber-500/40 transition-colors duration-200">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">SEO roadmap</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-processing="default">Technical fixes, content priorities, and link opportunities, sequenced by impact and effort. Updated quarterly.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">Roadmap sequenced by impact-vs-effort scoring: each item ranked, each ranking traceable to the data behind it. Refreshed quarterly when the data shifts.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">Priorities ranked by impact and effort. Updated every quarter.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 p-6 hover:border-amber-500/40 transition-colors duration-200">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Strategy memos</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" data-processing="default">When something needs your attention, a competitor move or an algorithm update, you get a clear memo with what to do about it.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">Memos function as strategic pulses between calls. Algorithm updates flagged with the strategic implication. Competitor moves flagged with the recommended response. Ranking shifts past significance flagged with what to investigate.</p>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">Strategic pulses between calls. When something matters, you hear about it before you'd notice it yourself.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 p-6 hover:border-amber-500/40 transition-colors duration-200">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 font-medium mb-2">Quarterly reports</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">Rankings, traffic, conversions, and what it means. Written for decision-makers, not analysts. Executive brief up front, data behind it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Portal block: where the strategic engagement lives -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <div class="mb-12 text-center">
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">The portal</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100">The receipt for the engagement.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 p-8 md:p-10 hover:border-amber-500/40 transition-colors duration-200">
        <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-lg" data-frame="default">
          Every engagement runs through one portal: contracts, change orders, invoices, files, milestones, approvals, notifications. One log-in, one source of truth, one place to find anything I've ever done for you.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-lg" style="display:none" data-frame="sun">
          Strategy you can watch happen. Each audit finding traces forward to the recommendation, the brief, the call decision, what got built or dropped. The portal is the engagement made visible.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-lg" style="display:none" data-frame="moon">
          The portal is the audit trail of the strategic engagement. Every recommendation logged, every decision dated, every brief tied to the call it came out of. Nothing the strategy work produces gets forgotten or argued about.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-lg mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-white/5" style="display:none" data-vibe="mountain">
          Magic-link sign-in (no passwords to leak). Sessions hashed. Files in encrypted storage. Activity log behind every action. Your data stays yours, end to end.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
      <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm mb-4">Ready to get found?</p>
      <a href="/contact?interest=marketing-strategy" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-4 border border-white/10 text-neutral-300 font-medium text-sm rounded-lg hover:border-amber-500/25 hover:text-amber-400 transition-colors duration-200">
        Let's talk strategy
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pricing (calibrated, no public tier ladder until ecosystem routing exists) -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <div>
        <p class="text-amber-400 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Pricing</p>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100 mb-8">Calibrated, not off the rack.</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-10">
          What you pay depends on how much strategic depth your business actually uses. Some clients want one focused audit and a clear roadmap; others want ongoing partnership at the marketing-director level. The engagement gets calibrated to that. Tell me where you're at and we'll figure out where you land.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact?interest=marketing-strategy" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-4 bg-amber-500 text-neutral-950 font-semibold text-sm rounded-lg hover:bg-amber-400 transition-colors duration-200">
          Tell me where you're at
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-32 px-6 surface-1">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-5xl text-neutral-100 mb-6">Know what you need to do next?</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-lg mb-10" data-processing="default">If the answer is "not really," that's exactly what this solves.</p>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-lg mb-10" style="display:none" data-processing="stars">Here's what the data says about your visibility: most businesses leave winnable organic positions uncontested. I'll show you yours, named and prioritized.</p>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-lg mb-10" style="display:none" data-processing="clouds">Let's figure out where people should find you, and make sure they actually do. No jargon, no dashboards you'll never check. Just clear direction.</p>
      <a href="/contact?interest=marketing-strategy" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-4 bg-amber-500 text-neutral-950 font-semibold text-sm rounded-lg hover:bg-amber-400 transition-colors duration-200">
        Build your roadmap
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
